WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.760
It's Saturday, November 7, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.720
Factory reset? In old rats,

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.370
two weeks on a drug halved an Alzheimer's-linked protein in their blood.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.400
Its first author compares it to Mufasa telling Simba: remember who you are.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.240
Meanwhile, a start-up says its AI solved a quantum maths puzzle open since 2008.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.380
And Mira Murati's lab is opening up Inkling 2 Small,

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.190
ranked the best open model outside China.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.430
Tesla now brands its chips SI, for super intelligence,

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.950
and promises 80 times today's compute.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.090
And China's Hubei province now covers deep brain s

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:59.210
timulation implants under basic medical insurance.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.060
An early trial gave failing livers engineered immune cells: 2 in 9 had setbacks,

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.270
versus 8 in 21.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.590
And in 61 adults,

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:14.470
a maker-funded longevity supplement made arteries more flexible and lowered blood pressure.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.210
Stanford scored resting brains from super ager to Alzheimer's-like,

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.470
flagging risk up to 12 years early.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.970
Across 41,000 US dogs,

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.330
the states where dogs die younger tend to match where people do.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.760
In wellbeing,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.940
brains of people with mental health diagnoses shifted gears less between rest and tasks.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.220
And in 100 couples, extra stress dented that evening's love,

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.250
but always-stressed people weren't less in love.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.190
Now, the catch. Poorer Australian kids are increasingly missing out on therapy,

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.770
even after seeing a GP.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.260
Asked to fix page numbers,

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.880
a Claude agent deleted a law professor's syllabus; luckily, backups saved the day.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.720
On the frontier, a remote-controlled humanoid cleaned a reporter's apartment,

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.920
climbing stairs like it was tipsy.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.630
A solar plane over the Canary Islands has flown more than 80 hours straight,

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:14.630
aiming for 100.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.180
And AgiBot's six shop robots did over 1,700 tasks in a day,

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.040
but two failed probation.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.710
No factory reset for us yet,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.180
but small fixes that hold up add up to more good years.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
